@startuml journaling_mechanism
!include ../../../00_SUPPLEMENTARY/diagrams_common/skin.puml
title Redo Journalling — Data and Metadata Journal Path

skinparam activity {
    DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
}

|Application|
start
:Write new data;

|Kernel / FS|
:1. **TXB** (Transaction Begin)
Write transaction descriptor to journal;

:2. Write **metadata + data**
to journal;

:3. **TXE** (Transaction End)
Persist commit after prior journal writes are durable;

:4. **Checkpoint**
Write data + metadata to their home locations;

:5. Reclaim journal space
only after the checkpoint is durable;

|Disk|
:Data saved!;
stop

legend right
**On CRASH / Power Failure:**

**Scenario 1:** Crash before TXE
→ Incomplete transaction → **Ignore**

**Scenario 2:** Crash after TXE
→ Complete transaction → **Replay**

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**ext4 Modes (different data-ordering contracts):**
|= Mode |= What is journalled |= Data ordering |
| journal | Metadata + Data | Data in the journal before commit |
| **ordered** | Metadata | Home data before metadata commit |
| writeback | Metadata only | No same data-before-commit ordering |

The flow above models the journal-data path.
Correct recovery assumes enforced write order and durable flushes.
Performance depends on workload and storage; no ranking is measured here.
endlegend

@enduml
